{
  "_doc": "Field envelopes and key wraps (packages/client-core/src/crypto/field.ts, envelope.ts, keyring.ts, identity.ts, asym.ts). AES-256-GCM is deterministic given the IV, so a reimplementation must both open each `envelope`/wrap and reproduce its `ct` from the recorded `iv`. Field v2: plaintext = JSON of `value`, ISO/IEC 7816-4 padded to `paddedLength` (0x80 then zeros; at least 32 bytes, then powers of two up to 1 KiB, then whole KiB); associated data = UTF-8 of JSON.stringify([\"atlas-field\", 2, entity, entity_id, field, scope, kid]). Field v3 (sync protocol 7, docs/decisions/0006): plaintext = JSON of [kind, field, value], padded as v2 but to at least 64 bytes (`padding_v3`); associated data = UTF-8 of JSON.stringify([\"atlas-field\", 3, wire_entity, entity_id, wire_field, scope, kid]), where wire_field is the tag or a public name. Field tags: tag_key = HKDF-SHA256(ikm key, no salt, info 'atlas-field-tag-v1', 32 bytes); tag = hex of the first 16 bytes of HMAC-SHA256(tag_key, UTF-8 of JSON.stringify([\"atlas-field-tag\", 1, entity_id, kind, field])). Field v1: JSON of value, unpadded, no associated data. PEK wrap v2: associated data JSON.stringify([\"atlas-pek-wrap\", 2, project_id]); the unbound form has none. project_key_id = hex of the first 16 bytes of SHA-256(\"atlas-pek-id-v1\" || pek). Signing key wrap: associated data JSON.stringify([\"atlas-signing-key-wrap\", 1, lowercase public key hex]). Sealed: X25519 with an ephemeral key, HKDF-SHA256(no salt, info 'atlas-seal-v1'), AES-256-GCM without associated data. Asserted by packages/client-core/src/crypto/envelope-vectors.test.ts and crates/atlas-client.",
